+## Bounded public cases and non-claims
+
+Default acquisition is four independent contexts per engine, sequential Chromium and Firefox:
+
+| Case | Controlled input and actual consumer predicate |
+| --- | --- |
+| `public-reordered24` | UTC 7 September 2026, 23:00; current Isha00:30, next-day Isha00:31. Actual completed receipt and DOM must agree on Isha,00:31,next date08-09-2026,UTC,epoch1788827460000,91minutes, literal `1h 31m left until Isha`, selected row/arc marker and compatible wall interval. |
+| `public-ordinary24` | Same UTC epoch with ordinary19:30 Isha. Actual receipt/DOM must select next-day Fajr05:00,epoch1788843600000,360minutes and literal `6h 0m left until Fajr`, with ordinary wall progress/arc semantics retained. |
+| `public-missing24` | Current record admitted, actual next-day HTTP response intentionally held before headers. Countdown must remain unavailable with no fabricated target/highlight; current timetable/date/arc stay present. This is absence of an admitted next record while ingress is pending, not a claim that a real provider failed. |
+| `public-recovery24` | Same unavailable state after observable typography/render settlement, then fulfill that actual pending native request. The original fetch/JSON/adoption path must eventually paint the coherent Isha91 endpoint at the identical frozen epoch under native scheduling. Private dirty flags and exclusive wakeup causality are not observed. |
+
+`public-reordered-offline` is an optional representative offline HTML consumer, explicitly selected with `--case-id`; it is not part of the default denominator. The offline file's delivered bytes are always checked regardless of this optional behavior case.
+
+Inputs/oracles were copied from the already-authored independent R0007 recipes, not generated from observed product results. The case manifest retains its source-recipe SHA. The only pre-boot clock change is a fixed Date ingress; performance, rAF, timers, renderer, boot, state adoption, and stored product data are not replaced or invoked by the probe. Every case uses a new private browser context with explicit coordinates and no granted permissions. It reads actual public HTML unchanged and never calls render/model or seeds a product record/cache. Browser-owned storage is ephemeral, separate from the user's profile.
+
+Provider HTTP responses are controlled before provider contact, using strict expected host/path/date/coordinates/method/school matching and native JSON consumption. Weather/radar requests fail through controlled ingress. Missing/recovery hold a response before headers; this narrower boundary is explicit and does not claim the historical body-stall timing subproof. Allowlisted actual site assets and the real source font CSS/font hosts use Playwright's ordinary `route.fetch(max_redirects=0)` followed by fulfillment with that original API response. Every HTTP redirect is refused before any redirect hop. There is no `route.continue_` escape; service workers are blocked and unknown external requests/WebSockets are blocked and recorded as nonpassing evidence. Original HTTP payload bytes are preserved, but this transport buffers responses and changes ingress timing. It is not a fully uninstrumented public network timing experiment.
+
+Readiness samples and prayer-DOM MutationObserver callbacks read `window.qaState().render`, the actual last completed render receipt, plus actual DOM. `qaState()` also computes other diagnostics and may touch a pending Moon getter; before/after material classes/href are retained, and diagnostic surface changes receive no scene-preservation credit. The probe never treats the diagnostic recomputation as a painted frame. Before unavailable-state capture/recovery release, it requires the authored font LINK's genuine trusted load/error receipt; successful load also requires its actual sheet, enabled state and authored `media=all`. It forces read-only geometry and awaits the real `document.fonts.ready` promise. Readiness alone does not prove the later font-event dispatch has completed. The exact R0007-owned early observer must also admit each relevant terminal face through its own typed `loadingdone`/`loadingerror` event and a captured native zero-timer receipt after dispatch. Missing receipts, outstanding deferred tasks, observed removal/restart or descriptor mutation fail closed. The observer is concatenated before the public INIT in one `add_init_script` call to guarantee installation order. The tool then observes unchanged actual render/geometry/font signatures across three native rAF callbacks, checking current observer settlement after each layout read and after final screenshot geometry. It repeats settlement before final capture. This is a static authored startup lifecycle protocol, not a universal future-font quiescence claim; a legitimate cached loaded face with no terminal event is conservatively unverified. These observations truthfully report `dirtyState: not-exposed`: neither the private dirty flag nor private loop state is accessible through the public diagnostics. The real 250ms wait plus subsequent settlement supports eventual recovery only; other natural wakeups are not excluded. No earliest/all-first-presented-frame claim, full-scene motion/Moon acceptance, exclusive-wakeup claim, or live-provider incidence is made.
+
+Acquisition credit is assigned only after successful actual observation export, required checkpoint membership, nonempty structurally complete PNG/WebM files, exact snapshot/receipt/geometry/screenshot-digest presentation bindings, browser identity and returned owned close calls. PNG structure/CRC/scanline and WebM bounded-element/track/block checks detect missing, malformed or truncated artifacts; actual frame decoding and pixel meaning remain independently reviewed. Launch entry, returned handles and every SDK close call are recorded. A launch exception before a handle returns has unknown process custody, even if no close call was possible; later acquisitions stop. SDK closure receipts do not claim an independent OS process census. Every attempted case retains its trace on failure, and producer exit remains nonzero for failed/unverified acquisition.
